From 49f25d028afe632af1c9fa6e809b3a89f765255f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gabriel Zim <info@zimcontent.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:15:47 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] fix(runner): taking control of the browser stops the
 agent's command

Taking control aborted only the path that presses and types as a person
does: reads, waits and the steps of a batch ran to their end (25 s in the
daemon). agent-browser's daemon runs one command at a time, the person's
relay included, so their input timed out after 5 s and was reported as
not delivered.

- Every act and batch call of the agent is aborted, queued ones too; a
  batch stops even on a step that tolerates a failure.
- A command already inside the daemon, which it finishes with no client,
  makes the person's input wait up to DAEMON_HOLD_MS instead of failing
  after 5 s.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
